---
description: TypeScript, React, Next.js and Node conventions
globs: **/*.ts,**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

- Strict TypeScript. No `any`; use `unknown` plus narrowing, or a real type. No `@ts-ignore` without a comment saying why.
- Validate external input (requests, env, API responses, forms) with zod at the boundary and infer types from the schema.
- React: function components, typed props. Use existing shadcn/ui components in `components/ui` before writing new ones. Style with Tailwind classes.
- Tests use the project's runner (vitest where present).
